# Development-only symlink farm pointing at the pinned DSH checkout.
# It is an artifact of this machine's layout, not part of the deliverable.
# BOTH packages need this: the entry was originally written for dsh-daily-work
# alone, so `packages/dsh-ipython/` stayed wholly untracked -- sources included
# -- for the entire build. A deliverable package whose source is not in the
# repository is not a deliverable, and a reader cannot tell an ignored build
# directory from a missing one.
packages/*/node_modules/
packages/*/lib/
**/.vite-temp/

# Junction farms created inside an evidence directory are the same
# machine-layout artifact as the package's own: they point at the pinned DSH
# checkout and must never be committed. A junction is a reparse point, so a
# checkout that recursed into one would copy the whole DSH tree.
qualification/results/**/node_modules/

# Per-session IPython kernel scratch (spill files, kernel.out/err). A runtime
# directory, not a deliverable: it is created by the kernel plugin under the
# configured root and holds nothing a reader needs. Left unignored it shows up as
# an untracked directory after any real kernel run, which is noise in a tree where
# untracked files have meant real defects twice today (G-SEAM-30, G-SEAM-42).
.ipython-kernels/
